<!-- wp:bwfd/endorsement -->
<figure class="wp-block-bwfd-endorsement"><blockquote><p class="bwfd-endorsement__quote">True kingdom impact doesn&rsquo;t stop with your professional reach; it multiplies through your family. In Biblical Wisdom for Dads, Stephen Parker offers a practical blueprint for cultivating healthy faith around your own dinner table, reminding us that discipling our children is a father&rsquo;s highest leadership responsibility. This book is essential training for any man who refuses to outsource his family&rsquo;s spiritual formation and instead wants to leave a lasting legacy that bears fruit for generations.</p></blockquote><figcaption class="bwfd-endorsement__who">Dave Ferguson, CEO of Exponential and author of many books, including Multiplier: How Healthy Leaders Create Lasting Impact.</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:bwfd/endorsement -->

<!-- wp:bwfd/endorsement -->
<figure class="wp-block-bwfd-endorsement"><blockquote><p class="bwfd-endorsement__quote">Timely, practical, and deeply rooted in Scripture, Stephen Parker&rsquo;s book, Biblical Wisdom for Dads, is an encouraging devotional guide for fathers in every season of life. At a time when families and our culture desperately need godly dads to embrace their God-given calling, it offers grace instead of guilt, helping fathers focus not on past failures but on the opportunities that lie ahead. Through honest stories, accessible wisdom, and short, engaging chapters, he shows that faithful fatherhood is both attainable and transformational. Whether you&rsquo;re an expectant dad, a new father, or a seasoned parent, this book will equip, encourage, and inspire you to lead your family with purpose, humility, and Christ-centred love.</p></blockquote><figcaption class="bwfd-endorsement__who">Dean Brenton, President, Impactus, Ontario, Canada.</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:bwfd/endorsement -->

<!-- wp:bwfd/endorsement -->
<figure class="wp-block-bwfd-endorsement"><blockquote><p class="bwfd-endorsement__quote">Reading this book felt less like turning pages and more like sitting down in a genuine bloke-to-bloke conversation. Stephen writes with honesty, humility and warmth, strongly drawing from Scripture without becoming over-spiritualised or preachy. The biblical principles are grounded, practical and deeply relatable to the everyday realities of being a dad. His blend of vulnerability, wisdom and practical application was confronting, comforting, and caused me to pause and reflect. Above all, this book reminded me that fatherhood is not just a biological role but a sacred stewardship&mdash;one of life&rsquo;s greatest spiritual challenges and highest callings.</p></blockquote><figcaption class="bwfd-endorsement__who">Michael Oon, Executive Coach and Founder of the Xtreme Character Challenge (XCC) for 4M Australia.</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:bwfd/endorsement -->

<!-- wp:bwfd/endorsement -->
<figure class="wp-block-bwfd-endorsement"><blockquote><p class="bwfd-endorsement__quote">With wit and wisdom, Stephen Parker invites men to consider what it means to be a parent in light of the character of our heavenly Father. Biblical Wisdom for Dads offers warm and insightful reflections on the Scriptures as an encouragement for the reader to see fatherhood as a both a source of deep blessing, as well as a great responsibility to share and show the gospel to others. This new resource will be a treasured guide for men&rsquo;s ministries, and a welcome devotional guide for those trying to be faithful to God and their family.</p></blockquote><figcaption class="bwfd-endorsement__who">Ross A. Lockhart, Professor of Mission Studies at Vancouver School of Theology, and Dean of St Andrew&rsquo;s Hall, Vancouver, Canada.</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:bwfd/endorsement -->

<!-- wp:bwfd/endorsement -->
<figure class="wp-block-bwfd-endorsement"><blockquote><p class="bwfd-endorsement__quote">Having grown up in a culture that was sadly - but too often aptly - described as &lsquo;the land of the absent father,&rsquo; Biblical Wisdom for Dads is a breath of fresh, renewing, hope-filled, encouraging, perspective-informing air! Stephen Parker has tapped into the beauty of fatherhood modelled by God, and through his own earthy experiences as both a son and a father, curated a collection of biblical fatherhood insights that will enrich soon-to-be, new, and experienced Dads.</p></blockquote><figcaption class="bwfd-endorsement__who">Adam Low, Lead Pastor, Real Life Christian Church, in Logan, Australia.</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:bwfd/endorsement -->

<!-- wp:bwfd/endorsement -->
<figure class="wp-block-bwfd-endorsement"><blockquote><p class="bwfd-endorsement__quote">I loved it! It was engaging, encouraging and challenging. I found myself highlighting sections, usually at least one in each chapter, that stood out to me. It helped me want to, and actually become, a better dad.</p></blockquote><figcaption class="bwfd-endorsement__who">Geoff Snook, Lead Pastor, The Lakes Church, Cairns, Australia.</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:bwfd/endorsement -->

<!-- wp:bwfd/endorsement -->
<figure class="wp-block-bwfd-endorsement"><blockquote><p class="bwfd-endorsement__quote">The greatest legacy a father can leave is not success, but faithfulness. Stephen Parker gently reminds us that discipling our children begins with our own ongoing walk with Jesus. Rich in biblical wisdom and practical encouragement, this is a thoughtful book for fathers who want to grow in Christ and lead their families with grace. I really appreciate the framing of fatherhood, rejecting both passivity and harshness, and instead rooting masculinity in the character of our Heavenly Father, something many men and families are deeply hungry for right now.</p></blockquote><figcaption class="bwfd-endorsement__who">Matthew C. Destry, Senior Pastor, Discovery Church, Melbourne, Australia.</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:bwfd/endorsement -->

<!-- wp:bwfd/endorsement -->
<figure class="wp-block-bwfd-endorsement"><blockquote><p class="bwfd-endorsement__quote">Reading Biblical Wisdom for Dads has been both enjoyable and insightful. Stephen combines biblical truth with his own lived experience to cover many principles of &ldquo;dadship&rdquo; that are often glossed over in parenting books. The shorter chapters allowed me, with each topic, to read and then take time to reflect personally and practically before moving on to the next chapter. I certainly recommend the book for dads, dads to be, and even old dads like me.</p></blockquote><figcaption class="bwfd-endorsement__who">Tim Hanna, OAM, Council Chair, Churches of Christ, QLD, formerly CEO of Compassion Australia and Senior Pastor of Gateway Baptist.</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:bwfd/endorsement -->
